Patch: 007-code-mode-nested
Reason: a code-mode model's script calls host tools as nested calls under ids of Codex's own that no rollout line carries and that name no exec, so a never tool's call was declined for good and a recovery answered a cut-off exec as if it had not run; the harness takes only the hooks (the module is code-mode.ts, written for AgentRun): it hands the module the harness's own log, journal and tail, wraps the app-server's request handler so a nested call is tied to its script and held for that script's line before the harness's own handler runs, overrides the dangling exec's output with the log's, and tells the module when a turn ends
Upstream: ours
Pins: code mode: an exec that calls a never host tool runs it exactly once
Pins: code mode: two nested calls of one exec (a Promise.all) each pass the barrier once, under the one exec, and run once
Pins: code mode: a never tool called after its exec yielded runs once, under the cell that is still running
Pins: code mode: a model that writes a new exec while a cell still runs: a never tool its new script calls is declined, not run
Pins: code mode: an unwatched answer's call in an earlier turn is not listed by a later turn's recovery
